The SSR investigation's logic
=============================

Its click on the scene: in the trace demonstration, the half-resolution pixel the trace starts from.

$[Import* std]
$[Import* render_lab_runtime]
$[Import* godot_ssr_values]
$[Import* godot_ssr_natives]
$[ImportAs rl_runtime rt]

A click on the scene, in the trace demonstration, picks the half-resolution pixel under it (`pickX`, `pickY`: the
trace runs at half the viewport's size), one pixel wide; elsewhere it picks nothing.
$[# scene {: {^ {click}
    [# size {rt::viewport}]
    {!if {= {rt::demo} "trace"}
        {'
            {setPickX {float {floor {/ {* {.u click} {.x size}} 2.0}}}}
            {setPickY {float {floor {/ {* {.v click} {.y size}} 2.0}}}}
            {setPickWidth 0.0}
            {setPickHeight 0.0}}
        {'}}} ClickHandler}]

A click on the thread-group inset picks the thread under it as P: its pixel in the group the frame drew
(`laneGroup`), at the SSR size that group is of.
$[# pickLane {: {^ {click}
    [# g {laneGroup}]
    [# i {min {truncate {* {.u click} 8.0}} 7}]
    [# j {min {truncate {* {.v click} 8.0}} 7}]
    {'
        {setPickX {float {+ {.x g} i}}}
        {setPickY {float {+ {.y g} j}}}
        {setPickWidth {float {.w g}}}
        {setPickHeight {float {.h g}}}}} ClickHandler}]

A click on the best-fit chart marks the stored length under it (the chart's lengths run from 0.05 to 1).
$[# pickFitLength {: {^ {click} {' {setFitLen {+ 0.05 {* 0.95 {.u click}}}}}} ClickHandler}]

A click on the fade chart marks the ray length under it (0 to 1 of the screen).
$[# pickFadeLength {: {^ {click} {' {setFadeProbe {.u click}}}} ClickHandler}]
